  [PASS] A4 DERIVED (EdS): a collapsing axis has l/l_ta = 4x(1-x) after turnaround, so the gas axis freezes (its accretion shock) at 4 x_s (1 - x_s) = s; the gate opens BEFORE the shock unless s >= l/l_ta(x*): 3/4 for a forming sheet, 8/9 for a forming filament, 1 for a halo (always open).  At the self-similar cold-accretion stand-off s = 0.347 the pre-shock gas reaches x_s = 0.904 > 3/4: the baryon reading opens the gate in forming sheets too
